 questions jsonb := $q$[{"n":1,"marks":2,"text":"In column H (Name (Proper)) write every Employee Name in proper case without extra spaces, using the PROPER and TRIM functions (for example \"  rAMESH  kumar SHARMA \" becomes \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\").","solution":"**TRIM** removes spaces at the start and end and leaves one space between words. **PROPER** makes the first letter of every word capital and the rest small. One function can go inside another.\n1. Click **H2** and type **=PROPER(TRIM(B2))** → Enter (\"  rAMESH  kumar SHARMA \" → \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\").\n2. Double-click the fill handle of H2 to fill down to **H201**.\n\nAlso: **UPPER** makes all capitals, **LOWER** all small letters.\n\nChecked: the exact text (capital letters matter here) in every cell H2:H201.","criteria":[{"column":"H","caseSensitive":true}]},{"n":2,"marks":1,"text":"In column I (Joining Year) find the year of joining from the Joining Date using the YEAR function.","solution":"A date in Excel is a number (days since 1 Jan 1900) shown in date format. **YEAR**, **MONTH** and **DAY** take out one part of it.\n1. Click **I2** and type **=YEAR(E2)** → Enter (16-07-2018 → 2018).\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **I201**.\n\nIf you see a date like 10-07-1905 instead of 2018, the cell has a date format: HOME → Number Format ▾ → **General**.\n\nChecked: the year in every cell I2:I201.","criteria":[{"column":"I"}]},{"n":3,"marks":2,"text":"In column J (DA) find DA = Basic Pay × DA Rate given in cell T2, rounded to 0 decimal places with ROUND. Use an absolute reference ($T$2) so the formula can be filled down.","solution":"When a formula is filled down, every reference moves one row: F2 becomes F3, F4... A **$** sign stops it moving. **$T$2** always points to T2 (press **F4** after typing T2 to add the $ signs).\n1. Click **J2** and type **=ROUND(F2*$T$2,0)** → Enter (24500 × 55% = 13475).\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **J201**.\n\nWithout the $ signs J3 would use T3 (empty), so every DA below row 2 would be 0.\n\nChecked: the DA in every cell J2:J201.","criteria":[{"column":"J"}]},{"n":4,"marks":2,"text":"In column K (Allowance) find the Allowance of every employee's Post from the table S6:T10 using VLOOKUP. Posts not in the table (Peon, Driver) must show 0: use IFERROR.","solution":"**=VLOOKUP(lookup_value, table, column_number, FALSE)** looks for the value in the first column of the table and returns the value from the given column. FALSE = exact match.\n1. Click **K2** and type **=IFERROR(VLOOKUP(D2,$S$6:$T$10,2,FALSE),0)** → Enter (LDC → 2000).\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **K201**.\n\nPeon and Driver are not in the table, so VLOOKUP gives **#N/A**; **IFERROR(value, 0)** shows 0 instead. The table needs $ signs so it does not move down when filled.\n\nChecked: every cell K2:K201.","criteria":[{"column":"K"}]},{"n":5,"marks":1,"text":"In column L (Gross Salary) find Gross Salary = Basic Pay + DA + Allowance.","solution":"1. Click **L2** and type **=F2+J2+K2** (or =SUM(F2,J2,K2)) → Enter (24500 + 13475 + 2000 = 39975).\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **L201**.\n\nChecked: every cell L2:L201.","criteria":[{"column":"L"}]},{"n":6,"marks":2,"text":"In column M (Rank) find the rank of every employee by Gross Salary (highest = 1) using the RANK function.","solution":"**=RANK(number, list, [order])** gives the position of a number in a list: order 0 or left out = highest gets 1.\n1. Click **M2** and type **=RANK(L2,$L$2:$L$201)** → Enter.\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **M201**.\n\nThe list must be absolute ($L$2:$L$201); otherwise it slides down and the ranks go wrong. Two equal salaries get the same rank.\n\nChecked: every cell M2:M201.","criteria":[{"column":"M"}]},{"n":7,"marks":2,"text":"In column N (Emp Code) make a code of the first 3 letters of the Department in capital letters, a hyphen, and the last 3 characters of the Emp ID (for example Revenue, RJ26001 → \"REV-001\"). Use UPPER, LEFT, RIGHT and &.","solution":"**LEFT(text, n)** takes n characters from the left, **RIGHT(text, n)** from the right, **MID(text, start, n)** from the middle. **&** joins text (same as CONCATENATE).\n1. Click **N2** and type **=UPPER(LEFT(C2,3))&\"-\"&RIGHT(A2,3)** → Enter (REV-001).\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **N201**.\n\nSame result: =CONCATENATE(UPPER(LEFT(C2,3)),\"-\",RIGHT(A2,3)).\n\nChecked: the exact code (capital letters matter) in every cell N2:N201.","criteria":[{"column":"N","caseSensitive":true}]},{"n":8,"marks":2,"text":"In Q2 find the total Gross Salary of the Education department using SUMIF, and in Q3 the total Gross Salary of LDCs of the Revenue department using SUMIFS.","solution":"**=SUMIF(range, criteria, sum_range)** adds the rows that meet one condition. **=SUMIFS(sum_range, range1, criteria1, range2, criteria2)** needs every condition; note the sum range comes first in SUMIFS.\n1. **Q2**: =SUMIF(C2:C201,\"Education\",L2:L201) → 2264120.\n2. **Q3**: =SUMIFS(L2:L201,C2:C201,\"Revenue\",D2:D201,\"LDC\") → 436470.\n\nChecked: Q2 and Q3, both with formulas.","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"Q2","equals":2264120,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"Q3","equals":436470,"formula":true}]},{"n":9,"marks":2,"text":"In Q4 find the 3rd highest Gross Salary using LARGE, and in Q5 the 2nd lowest Gross Salary using SMALL.","solution":"**=LARGE(range, k)** gives the k-th highest value, **=SMALL(range, k)** the k-th lowest. LARGE(range,1) is the same as MAX, SMALL(range,1) as MIN.\n1. **Q4**: =LARGE(L2:L201,3) → 72975.\n2. **Q5**: =SMALL(L2:L201,2) → 27590.\n\nChecked: Q4 and Q5, both with formulas.","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"Q4","equals":72975,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"Q5","equals":27590,"formula":true}]},{"n":10,"marks":2,"text":"In Q6 find the name of the highest paid employee using INDEX and MATCH (with MAX).","solution":"**MATCH(value, range, 0)** tells the position of a value in a range (0 = exact). **INDEX(range, position)** gives the value at that position. Together they look up in any direction, which VLOOKUP cannot (VLOOKUP only looks to the right).\n1. Click **Q6** and type **=INDEX(H2:H201,MATCH(MAX(L2:L201),L2:L201,0))** → Enter → Mahendra Singh Rathore.\n\nMAX finds the highest gross, MATCH finds its row number in the list, INDEX takes the name from that row.\n\nChecked: Q6 with a formula (the name from column B also counts).","criteria":[{"rule":"anyOf","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"Q6","equals":"Mahendra Singh Rathore","formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"Q6","equals":" mahendra singh RATHORE","formula":true}]}]},{"n":11,"marks":2,"text":"In Q7 count the employees who joined in 2015 or later (use column I with COUNTIF), and in Q8 count the employees without a mobile number using COUNTBLANK.","solution":"1. **Q7**: =COUNTIF(I2:I201,\">=2015\") → 98.\n2. **Q8**: =COUNTBLANK(G2:G201) → 18 (COUNTBLANK counts the empty cells).\n\nRemember: COUNT = cells with numbers, COUNTA = cells that are not empty, COUNTBLANK = empty cells.\n\nChecked: Q7 and Q8, both with formulas.","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"Q7","equals":98,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"Q8","equals":18,"formula":true}]},{"n":12,"marks":2,"text":"Using VLOOKUP with the Emp ID \"RJ26150\", find in Q9 the Gross Salary and in Q10 the Post of that employee from the table A2:L201.","solution":"Count the columns of the table from its first column: A = 1, B = 2, C = 3, D = 4 ... L = 12.\n1. **Q9**: =VLOOKUP(\"RJ26150\",A2:L201,12,FALSE) → 50860.\n2. **Q10**: =VLOOKUP(\"RJ26150\",A2:L201,4,FALSE) → UDC.\n\nAlways write FALSE (exact match) when looking up an ID or a name; TRUE (approximate) needs a sorted list and can give a wrong row.\n\nChecked: Q9 and Q10, both with formulas.","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"Q9","equals":50860,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"Q10","equals":"UDC","formula":true}]},{"n":13,"marks":1,"text":"Format the Gross Salary range L2:L201 as Accounting Number Format with the ₹ symbol and 2 decimal places.","solution":"1. Select **L2:L201** (click L2, then **Ctrl+Shift+↓**).\n2. HOME → **Accounting Number Format (₹)**. It shows 2 decimal places: ₹ 39,975.00.\n\n(Ctrl+1 → Number → **Currency**, Symbol ₹, Decimal places 2 also counts.)\n\nChecked: L2:L201 in Accounting or Currency format with ₹ and 2 decimals.","criteria":[{"rule":"cells","range":"L2:L201","props":{"numberFormat":["Accounting","Currency"],"currency":[null,"₹"],"decimals":[2]}}]},{"n":14,"marks":1,"text":"Freeze the top row of the sheet so the headings stay visible while scrolling.","solution":"1. VIEW → **Freeze Panes ▾** → **Freeze Top Row**.\n\n(Clicking A2 and choosing Freeze Panes does the same.)\n\nChecked: panes frozen below row 1.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"freeze","equals":"A2"}]},{"n":15,"marks":1,"text":"With Conditional Formatting highlight the Top 10 Gross Salaries in L2:L201 with Green Fill with Dark Green Text.","solution":"1. Select **L2:L201**.\n2. HOME → **Conditional Formatting ▾** → **Top/Bottom Rules** → **Top 10 Items...**\n3. Keep **10**, choose **Green Fill with Dark Green Text** → **OK**.\n\nChecked: a Top 10 rule with the green style on L2:L201.","criteria":[{"rule":"anyOf","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"L2:L201","type":"top","value":10,"style":"greenDarkGreen"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"L1:L201","type":"top","value":10,"style":"greenDarkGreen"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"L2:L201","type":"top","value":"10","style":"greenDarkGreen"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"L1:L201","type":"top","value":"10","style":"greenDarkGreen"}}]}]}]$q$::jsonb;
 cells jsonb; model_cells jsonb; working jsonb; model jsonb;
begin
 if exists (select 1 from public.excel_efficiency_tests where slug = 'efficiency-test-5') then raise notice 'EXCEL EFFICIENCY TEST 5 already exists'; return; end if;

 select fixed || jsonb_object_agg(chr(65 + i) || (r + 2), pg_temp.excel_cell(employees->r->i, null, case when i = 4 then 'ShortDate' else 'General' end)) into cells
 from generate_series(0, jsonb_array_length(employees) - 1) r, generate_series(0, 6) i where jsonb_typeof(employees->r->i) <> 'null';
 working := jsonb_build_object('schemaVersion', 1, 'language', 'English', 'rows', 201, 'cols', 20, 'cells', cells);
 perform public.assert_excel_efficiency_working_matter(working);

 select cells || jsonb_object_agg(ref, cell) into model_cells from (
   select t.key || (r + 2) as ref, pg_temp.excel_cell(vals->t.key->r, replace(t.value, '#', (r + 2)::text)) as cell from jsonb_each_text(templates) t, generate_series(0, 199) r
   union all select key, pg_temp.excel_cell(value->1, value->>0) from jsonb_each(summary_formulas)) x;
 select model_cells || jsonb_object_agg('L' || r, (model_cells->('L' || r)) || '{"numberFormat":"Accounting","currency":null,"decimals":2}'::jsonb)
   into model_cells from generate_series(2, 201) r;
 model := jsonb_build_object('schemaVersion', '3', 'rows', 201, 'cols', 20, 'cells', model_cells, 'merges', '[]'::jsonb,
   'sheet', $q${"name":"Sheet1","freeze":"A2","conditionalFormats":[{"range":"L2:L201","type":"top","value":10,"style":"greenDarkGreen"}]}$q$::jsonb, 'operations', '[]'::jsonb, 'savedAt', '2026-11-08T00:00:00.000Z');
 perform public.assert_excel_efficiency_document_schema(model);

 insert into public.excel_efficiency_tests (slug, title, language, status, created_by, sequence, auto_publish_results)
 values ('efficiency-test-5', 'EFFICIENCY TEST 5', 'English', 'draft', admin_id, 5, true) returning id into t_id;
 insert into public.excel_efficiency_versions (test_id, version_number, title, language, description, instructions_markdown, question_count, maximum_marks,
   duration_options, passing_marks, working_matter_snapshot, created_by, delivery_pdf, delivery_onscreen, student_question_toggle, model_answer_snapshot)
 values (t_id, 1, 'EFFICIENCY TEST 5', 'English', 'Salary sheet of 200 employees: $ references, VLOOKUP, IFERROR, RANK, INDEX/MATCH, text and date functions',
   $q$1. Carefully read the instructions and solve the questions accordingly.
2. All questions are mandatory.
3. The sheet has 200 employees (rows 2 to 201). Fill a formula in row 2, then double-click the fill handle to copy it down to row 201.
4. **Maximum marks** and question-wise marks are shown with the questions.
5. Complete each task directly in the spreadsheet. Any method is fine (formula, drag and fill, Flash Fill or typing): the answer in the cells is what is checked.$q$, 15, 25, array[600, 900, 1200], 9, working, admin_id, false, true, true, model) returning id into v_id;
 update public.excel_efficiency_tests set current_version_id = v_id, current_version_number = 1 where id = t_id;

 for item in select value from jsonb_array_elements(questions) loop
  crit := '[]'::jsonb;
  for c in select value from jsonb_array_elements(item->'criteria') loop
   if c ? 'column' then crit := crit || pg_temp.column_checks(vals, c->>'column', coalesce((c->>'caseSensitive')::boolean, false));
   else crit := crit || jsonb_build_array(c);
   end if;
  end loop;
  insert into public.excel_efficiency_questions (version_id, question_number, instruction, marks, display_order, solution)
  values (v_id, (item->>'n')::int, item->>'text', (item->>'marks')::numeric, (item->>'n')::int, item->>'solution') returning id into q_id;
  insert into public.excel_efficiency_grading_rules (version_id, question_id, exact_target, expected_operation, expected_value, allocated_marks, additional_criteria)
  values (v_id, q_id, 'hand-written', 'rule-criteria', 'null'::jsonb, (item->>'marks')::numeric, crit);
 end loop;
end $mig$;

-- Check: the model answer scores the full marks of every question, the untouched sheet 0.
select q.question_number, q.marks,
  public.excel_efficiency_score_question(v.model_answer_snapshot, v.id, q.id, q.marks) as model,
  public.excel_efficiency_score_question(public.excel_efficiency_initial_editor_document(v.working_matter_snapshot), v.id, q.id, q.marks) as untouched
from public.excel_efficiency_tests t join public.excel_efficiency_versions v on v.id = t.current_version_id
join public.excel_efficiency_questions q on q.version_id = v.id where t.slug = 'efficiency-test-5' order by q.question_number;

commit;
